      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "`--fix` can report success without fixing the top-level field",
      "description": "When `--fix` receives a finding, it treats a successful `updateFrontmatterField` call as resolved and removes the finding from `remaining` without revalidating the file. The writer searches all frontmatter lines for a matching key, including nested YAML fields, while the parser ignores nested fields. For example, if a required top-level `status` is absent but a nested `metadata.status` exists, the writer can update the nested value; the validator will still see the top-level field as missing, but this command can exit 0. Revalidate after applying fixes, or ensure the write targets the top-level field before marking a finding resolved.",
